WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Here's a square photo.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:06.580
Each side is x centimetres,
so its area is x squared.

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.100
Now enlarge it.

4
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.280
Make it three centimetres wider
and three centimetres taller.

5
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.160
A student writes the new
area as x squared plus nine.

6
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.710
After all, three squared is nine.

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.560
So is the new area really
just x squared plus nine?

8
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.520
Or has something gone missing?

9
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.100
In this mission, you'll
collect like terms,

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.850
and see why x squared
and x can't be combined.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.580
You'll expand two brackets by multiplying
every term in the first bracket by every

12
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.040
term in the second.

13
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.650
And you'll use a grid as an area picture,

14
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.270
splitting a rectangle into
four smaller rectangles.

15
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: find the area
of the enlarged square.
